# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
/migrate

# Development tools built from the tools/ module by `make tools`
/bin/

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# sqlc-generated code under internal/platform/postgres/generated is deliberately
# COMMITTED, not ignored: a fresh clone must build without sqlc installed, and a
# migration that silently changes a Go type should show up in code review.
# `make generate` regenerates it; CI runs `sqlc diff` to prove it's current.

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/
